From: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(darwin): client control API and relay paths on macOS

Builds on the client-mode control API (Linux) and relay paths
(NAME@HOST:PORT, POSIX bind) and wires both into the Darwin client:

- Control API: --control-port / [Control] Listen serve get_status (per
  path "iface" and "status"), get_stats, get_build_info and
  get_reorder_stats in client mode on macOS. control_socket.c is plain
  POSIX + libevent, so the Darwin CLI compiles it from
  src/platform/linux/ rather than a copy (moving it to src/platform/posix/
  is a pure rename for a follow-up). No RX offload counters on Darwin.
- Relay paths: a NAME@HOST:PORT slot is not IP_BOUND_IF-pinned (its
  socket is routed normally to the relay), gets the relay set on its
  transport, and is skipped by everything that treats a slot name as an
  interface: the scoped server pins (#F1) at setup, re-add and
  reactivate, the reactivate re-pin, and the route monitor's
  interface-gone fallback and periodic resync (which would otherwise drop
  it as "interface not present"). Interface paths are unchanged.
- Tests: test_control_socket (client mode included) now runs in the
  Darwin ctest set; test_bind_posix_socket already does, and covers the
  relay bind and the spec parser there.

Signed-off-by: Tiger Kaovilai <passawit.kaovilai@gmail.com>
